  "notes": [
    "Generated minifig MF07_firefighter (Firefighter) written by scripts/build_minifigs.py: parts picked by constant name from data/categories/parts/minifig, placements composed from LDCad shadow connector frames (data/offLibShadow via pyldraw3). Frame: torso origin at the neck, -Y up, face along -Z, figure's left +X, feet at y=+72.",
    "Seven revolute joints shared by every catalog figure: neck (head + headgear, vertical axis through the neck pin), shoulder_l/r (arm about the torso socket axis, tilted 9.79 deg), wrist_l/r (hand + held item about the arm socket axis, 45 deg; parent = arm), hip_l/r (leg about the hip pin axis through y=44).",
    "Sign convention by meaning (checked with the evaluator, kinematics.json): neck + = face turns to the figure's left; shoulder + = arm forward/up; wrist + = held item's tip rolls outward; hip + = leg forward (+pi/2 seated). Mirrored sides therefore have mirrored axes.",
    "Ranges: neck and wrists +/-pi, shoulders +/-4pi (free spin for arm circles/swimming), hips +/-pi/2. The real joints turn freely; these ranges are catalog choices, not measured stops.",
    "Torso, hips and back items are static. Whole-figure motion in the animation (move_forward, move_left, move_up, turn, pitch, roll on the controller, pivot = hip-axis centre (0,44,0)) is staging, not a mechanism: it parents the model root and is not part of this plan.",
